  {
   "mark": "town",
   "id": "quarter_view",
   "say": "West of the street the Roman houses stand open to the sky. The doors are gone, and the shutters, and most of the roof beams; what couldn't be carried off was burned where it stood. Someone has scratched a word into the plaster of the nearest wall, in Gallic, in Latin letters. It isn't a kind one."
